I created this project begainer friendly basics of IoT development. 🔌 Proxy support is an important part of this embedded system. Since I live in China, I have included proxy support in most projects so I can use Firebase's free tier. In some cases, I will also provide a proxyless version of the code.

[Note: ⚠️ Internal and external links can change anytime, be carefull while using them]

🛠️ Tools:
    1. Coding: VS Code with the PlatformIO plugin
    2. Firebase Spark plan (free tier): https://firebase.google.com/pricing


📁 All project files are in the "/archive" folder. I will try to keep the projects in sequence. Copy the code from the necessary file in "/archive" to "src\main.cpp" to upload and test it. Below, I briefly explain each project.

# \archive\a_1_single_led_control
    💡 Controls a single LED. Using a proxy is not mandatory, but I needed one to communicate with the Firebase API from China. The proxy was a VPN running on my local PC.
     step 1: 
        1. In Firebase https://firebase.google.com/pricing creat a project 
        2. Creat "Users" in "Authentication"
        3. set "Rules" in 'Realtime Database' using given User Id, for read and write permission Example:
                { "rules": 
                    { 
                    ".read": "auth.uid === 'IRBYumRJO7W**************'", 
                    ".write": "auth.uid === 'IRBYumRJO7W**************'" 
                    } 
                }
        4. Import or make the 'Data', example 
            \archive\a_1_single_led_control\led-esp32.json
        5. From "Your App" copy "SDK setup and configuration"

    step 2: 🚀
        1. Modify .cpp code according to wifi, and "SDK setup and configuration"
        2. Load to esp32
    step 3: 🔄 Change the value in 'Realtime Database' 'Data' value and see the change in esp32, example 12:0 LED off, 12:1 LED on 💡

